  "worked_solution": "The distance between the vector $x$ and the vector space $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by $\u2016x-\\overset{^}{x}\u2016$, where $\\overset{^}{x}$ in the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{span}{b}.$\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{b\\cdot x}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-2)+(-1)(-2)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-2-2+2}{1+1+1+1}b \\\\  & =-b \\\\  & =-1[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016x-\\overset{^}{x}\u2016 & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{((-2)-(-1))^{2}+(2-1)^{2}+((-2)-(-1))^{2}+((-2)-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
